doc/config/ - modular preamble
==============================

The report's preamble, split by concern so each piece is readable and
reusable in isolation. main.tex pulls in only preamble.tex.

    preamble.tex    orchestrator: \input the modules below, in order
    package.tex     every \usepackage EXCEPT hyperref
    colors.tex      figure palette + hyperlink colours (needs xcolor)
    tikz.tex        TikZ libraries + the shared node/edge styles
    macros.tex      document-level helper commands (\cmd, \reg, \byte, ...)
    hyperref.tex    links, PDF metadata, and the viewer bookmark tree

Load order matters
------------------
package -> colors -> tikz -> macros -> hyperref. hyperref MUST come last (it
redefines cross-referencing internals) and after cite/url, which is why it is
kept out of package.tex.

The bookmark tree ("side TOC in the PDF viewer") comes from hyperref's
bookmarks + pdfpagemode=UseOutlines in hyperref.tex; no in-document
\tableofcontents is used.
